WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.656
Perda's heart pounded. Despite Darb's shouts, Zann was still holding on to the skull.

2
00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:09.826
The energy around him was becoming more violent with every passing second.

3
00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:15.393
If she and the others didn't convince him to drop that skull, its power might destroy him.

4
00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:18.791
Zann glared at a tiny dragon that was harassing Zing.

5
00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:22.091
"Stop!" he intoned, pointing at it.

6
00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:23.513
Blast!

7
00:00:23.514 --> 00:00:29.511
The spell singed Zing's tail, and with a yelp, the pet dragon dived behind a pile of rubble.

8
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:33.042
"We've got to stop Zann!" Perda cried.

9
00:00:33.043 --> 00:00:36.412
Without waiting for a response, she leaped at Zann.

10
00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:39.390
"Oof!" he grunted as she tackled him.

11
00:00:39.391 --> 00:00:45.461
The skull bounced out of Zann's grip and rolled away, coming to rest against the candlestick he had dropped.

12
00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:53.706
Zann's eyes had stopped glowing, and he lay on the floor for a moment, breathing hard. Then he sat up and looked around the room.

13
00:00:53.707 --> 00:00:57.292
"Zann?" Darb said cautiously. "Are you okay?"

14
00:00:57.293 --> 00:01:02.185
Zann didn't respond. Climbing to his feet, he stepped toward the skull.

15
00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:05.729
"No!" Perda shouted. "Don't touch it!"

16
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.025
"Please, Zann," Gliss said, sobbing.

17
00:01:10.026 --> 00:01:17.526
Grabbing the candlestick, Zann lifted it over his head and brought it down as hard as he could, smashing the skull to bits.

18
00:01:17.527 --> 00:01:22.939
"No person should ever hold that much power," Zann said in a shaky voice.

19
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.618
He smiled weakly. "I guess now I know how Morb feels."

20
00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:34.038
Just then a small band of trolls, grunting heavily, rushed through the doorway and into the room.

21
00:01:34.039 --> 00:01:39.954
"Oh no!" Perda cried. "It looks like some of the trolls are still under Morb's control!"

22
00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:43.683
"How are we going to get out of here?" Gliss exclaimed.

23
00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:49.847
Zann smiled. "Magic—how else?" He waved toward the remains of the machine.

24
00:01:49.848 --> 00:01:53.437
"Morb can't track us anymore, remember?"

25
00:01:53.438 --> 00:01:56.641
Gliss quickly zapped herself and Darb away.

26
00:01:56.642 --> 00:02:00.870
Perda grinned and rubbed her fingers together. "Zap."

27
00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:03.260
She landed in a deserted hallway.

28
00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:09.597
Her friends were nowhere in sight, which was not surprising since there hadn't been enough time to agree on a destination.

29
00:02:09.598 --> 00:02:12.669
But that didn't matter now that they could use magic.

30
00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:18.572
Perda was about to summon a message moth to track down the others when she heard loud voices nearby.

31
00:02:18.573 --> 00:02:24.342
Curious, she stepped toward the nearest window and discovered that she was on the second floor.

32
00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:27.367
Another machine stood in the courtyard below.

33
00:02:27.368 --> 00:02:31.253
"That must be the magic-sucking machine," thought Perda.

34
00:02:31.254 --> 00:02:35.403
Standing near the machine were two people—Slib and Morb.

35
00:02:35.404 --> 00:02:41.231
"You've failed me!" Morb shouted. His face was twisted with anger.

36
00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:45.417
"I'm sorry, Your Majesty," Slib whined.

37
00:02:45.418 --> 00:02:49.847
"I searched all night, but I couldn't catch any leeches.

38
00:02:49.848 --> 00:02:56.198
Every time I displaced the water in the river, they wriggled into the mud before I could catch—"

39
00:02:56.199 --> 00:03:01.579
"First someone tampers with my trolls, and now this!" Morb interrupted him.

40
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:11.399
"Schoolchildren all over Magica know how to catch those leeches, and yet you can't manage to bring me the single one I require?"

41
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.189
Perda frowned, puzzled. Why did Morb need a single local leech?

42
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.703
Morb sent a sizzle of energy at Slib.

43
00:03:18.704 --> 00:03:24.593
The energy surrounded Slib for a second, but as far as Perda could tell, it didn't do anything to him.

44
00:03:24.594 --> 00:03:32.495
Then Morb snapped his fingers. Perda could hear a loud growl, and a strange striped creature stepped into view.

45
00:03:32.496 --> 00:03:39.603
Slib looked at it. "Your Majesty," he said. "What . . . is . . . that?"

46
00:03:39.604 --> 00:03:45.468
"It comes from a world with no magic," Morb said with an evil chuckle.

47
00:03:45.469 --> 00:03:55.173
"Of course, for an experienced Magician such as you, that shouldn't be a problem. There's just one minor detail . . ."

48
00:03:55.174 --> 00:03:58.067
"Your Majesty?" said Slib.

49
00:03:58.068 --> 00:04:08.049
Morb smirked. "I put a Dousing spell on you—you aren't able to use any magic," he said. Then he laughed nastily.

50
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:13.471
Perda ducked out of sight as Slib's screams of terror echoed through the palace.

51
00:04:13.472 --> 00:04:17.075
Meanwhile Zann tiptoed along a windowless corridor.

52
00:04:17.076 --> 00:04:21.617
He knew he should look for his friends, but he couldn't stop thinking about his grandfather.

53
00:04:21.618 --> 00:04:24.416
Boz was somewhere in the palace right now.

54
00:04:24.417 --> 00:04:29.773
He thought about summoning a spy fly to help him locate Boz. But that would take too long.

55
00:04:29.774 --> 00:04:34.297
Then he remembered a spell that he had learned in Family Spells class a few months earlier.

56
00:04:34.298 --> 00:04:41.132
Closing his eyes, he focused on a memory from when he was five years old—Boz had taken him to the ocean for the day.

57
00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:48.050
The two of them were watching a group of giant sea dragons romp in the waves, and Zann was mesmerized by the enormous creatures.

58
00:04:48.051 --> 00:04:53.788
After a few minutes, he realized his grandfather had been watching him instead of the dragons.

59
00:04:53.789 --> 00:04:57.117
"Why are you looking at me?" Zann asked.

60
00:04:57.118 --> 00:05:02.637
Boz smiled warmly. "You're much more interesting to me than those dragons."

61
00:05:02.638 --> 00:05:11.348
Zann focused on Boz's face from this exact moment, making sure he got every detail right. "Expand," he murmured.

62
00:05:11.349 --> 00:05:14.799
The image expanded so that Zann could see the background.

63
00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.252
Boz was sitting in a stone cell, looking worried.

64
00:05:18.253 --> 00:05:19.730
It was working!

65
00:05:19.731 --> 00:05:23.784
Zann continued to focus, and the image grew larger and larger.

66
00:05:23.785 --> 00:05:29.558
Soon he could see the entire dungeon, and then he could see a stairwell leading to it.

67
00:05:29.559 --> 00:05:37.288
The image continued to expand until it contained the entire palace, including Zann's own current location.

68
00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:44.539
He quickly studied this three-dimensional map and memorized Boz's location five floors below.

69
00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.333
"Zap!" Zann said.

70
00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.825
He landed in the dark, in the middle of a flight of steps.

71
00:05:50.826 --> 00:05:54.179
Below he could see light and hear voices.

72
00:05:54.180 --> 00:06:01.023
Hurrying in their direction, Zann found himself in a long corridor lit by torches and lined with many cells.

73
00:06:01.024 --> 00:06:04.982
In every one, red hair glowed in the torchlight.

74
00:06:04.983 --> 00:06:07.743
"Zann?" a familiar voice called out.

75
00:06:07.744 --> 00:06:15.341
Zann smiled. "Boz!" he shouted, rushing toward his grandfather's cell.

